    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d429-a1">

                <pb facs="0444" n="346" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg346"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sanderson to Mr. Choate.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-07-21"><hi rendition="#italic">July 21,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Ambassador</hi>: We have a telegram from our
                    acting consul-general at Shanghai dated 11.50 this morning. He reports a message
                    from the governor of Shantung yesterday that trustworthy news has been received
                    from Pekin of the safety of all the ministers, and that the Government is
                    arranging for their rescue. * * *</p>
                <p>I am told by our experts that with relays of hordes laid down a courier from
                    Pekin might possibly just manage to cover the distance from thence to Teinanfu,
                    the capital of Shantung, in two days; but it seems to me that we have no
                    security that Mr. Conger’s message was written the day the messenger left.</p>
                <p>Believe me, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. H. Sanderson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
